# WARNING: `scripts/sdd-workspace` REWRITES this file to a bare `*` on every run,
# and `scripts/task-brief` calls it. If you find it clobbered, restore this content —
# and note that already-tracked files stay tracked regardless, so the damage is only
# to records created after the clobber. `git add -f` is the reliable belt-and-braces
# when committing new ones.
#
# The SDD workspace is tracked, minus what is DERIVED from something already tracked.
# Everything here is per-plan: `.superpowers/sdd/<plan-basename>/`.
#
# Kept: `progress.md` (the ledger — rulings and their reasons), `task-N-report.md`
# (what the implementer did and what it found wrong with its brief), and
# `task-N-review.md` / `whole-branch-review.md` (findings and how each was verified).
# Those are original and exist nowhere else. See CLAUDE.md § The development record.
#
# Ignored below: task briefs are extracted mechanically from the plan by
# `scripts/task-brief`, and every `.diff` is regenerable from the two commits named
# in its filename. Tracking either would be storing a second copy of something git
# already holds — the defaults-file problem this project refuses elsewhere.

task-*-brief.md
*.diff
*.txt
